cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Sundew: an SSH/Telnet honeypot dataset with behavioural campaign attribution"
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
authors:
  - alias: Ap6pack
url: "https://ap6pack.github.io/dist/honeypot/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Ap6pack/Ap6pack.github.io"
license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - honeypot
  - cowrie
  - threat-intelligence
  - ssh
  - telnet
  - indicators-of-compromise
abstract: >-
  Observations from a single Cowrie SSH/Telnet honeypot on one AWS EC2
  instance, published continuously. Includes a tiered and aged indicator
  feed, per-address behavioural campaign attribution with terminal
  recordings, MITRE ATT&CK pattern matches, and captured malware metadata.

  Two properties matter when citing it. It is one sensor on one address, so
  it describes what happened to walk past rather than the internet. And its
  session- and event-weighted totals are dominated by a small number of
  hosts: one reconnaissance cluster accounts for roughly 80% of all sessions
  from five addresses, which is why the published figures are weighted by
  distinct source and the reconnaissance traffic is classified separately.
  See data/v1/feed/README.md for the methodology.
